@page "/"
@namespace MississippiSamples.Spring.Client.Pages

<PageTitle>Spring · a live Mississippi demo</PageTitle>
<main class="spring-home">
    <section class="spring-hero" aria-labelledby="welcome-heading">
        <div class="spring-hero-copy">
            <p class="spring-kicker">THE MISSISSIPPI FLAGSHIP DEMO</p>
            <h1 id="welcome-heading">Move money. <br/>See the system <br/><span>come to life.</span></h1>
            <p class="spring-intro">
                Open two fictional bank accounts, make a change and watch live balances
                and transactions follow. Every outcome comes from the running system.
            </p>
            <a class="spring-button spring-primary" href="/accounts">Start with two accounts <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
            <p class="spring-first-run">New here? Start with Ada and Grace, each with £500.</p>
        </div>
        <aside class="spring-flow" aria-label="How Mississippi handles a banking action">
            <div class="spring-flow-heading">
                <span>ONE ACTION. A LIVE OUTCOME.</span><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
            </div>
            <ol>
                <li>
                    <span class="spring-step">01</span>
                    <div>
                        <h2>You choose a task</h2>
                        <p>Deposit, withdraw or transfer money.</p>
                    </div>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <span class="spring-step">02</span>
                    <div>
                        <h2>The command is checked</h2>
                        <p>The domain accepts it or returns a reason.</p>
                    </div>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <span class="spring-step">03</span>
                    <div>
                        <h2>Events update the views</h2>
                        <p>Inlet brings balance and ledger projections to the browser.</p>
                    </div>
                </li>
            </ol>
            <p class="spring-flow-note">
                An accepted command and a refreshed projection are separate observations.
                You will see both in the demo.
            </p>
        </aside>
    </section>
    <section class="spring-task-section" aria-labelledby="tasks-heading">
        <div class="spring-section-heading">
            <h2 id="tasks-heading">What do you want to try?</h2>
            <p>Follow the first path, or explore a specific capability.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="spring-task-grid">
            <a class="spring-task" href="/accounts">
                <span class="spring-task-number">01 / START HERE</span>
                <h3>Prepare your accounts</h3>
                <p>Create the demo pair or open accounts using your own IDs.</p><span class="spring-task-next">Account commands <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></span>
            </a>
            <a class="spring-task" href="/operations">
                <span class="spring-task-number">02 / MOVE MONEY</span>
                <h3>Make a change. Verify it.</h3>
                <p>Deposit, withdraw and transfer. Follow balances, ledgers and saga outcomes.</p><span class="spring-task-next">Live projections &amp; sagas <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></span>
            </a>
            <a class="spring-task" href="/investigations">
                <span class="spring-task-number">03 / FOLLOW AN EVENT</span>
                <h3>Find a flagged deposit</h3>
                <p>A deposit above £10,000 triggers a separate investigation queue.</p><span class="spring-task-next">Event-driven effects <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></span>
            </a>
            <a class="spring-task" href="/auth-proof">
                <span class="spring-task-number">04 / TEST A BOUNDARY</span>
                <h3>Change who has access</h3>
                <p>Compare five local personas against authenticated, role and claim rules.</p><span class="spring-task-next">Generated authorization <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></span>
            </a>
        </div>
    </section>
    <section class="spring-context" aria-labelledby="context-heading">
        <div>
            <p class="spring-kicker">BUILT WITH MISSISSIPPI</p>
            <h2 id="context-heading">Inspect what makes it work.</h2>
        </div>
        <p>
            Generated commands connect the UI to an event-sourced domain. Reservoir holds client state.
            Inlet updates read projections. Sagas coordinate a transfer across accounts.
            Refraction provides the presentation controls and themes.
        </p>
        <a href="/scalar/v1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Explore the generated API ↗</a>
    </section>
</main>